Google today said it is <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/google-pay/wallet-available-ios-united-states/">bringing Google Wallet</a> to iOS in the United States, giving users a way to make payments and manage purchases across Google services.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/google-wallet-ios.jpg" alt="" width="1650" height="928" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078014" /><br/>
Google Wallet cannot be used for tap-to-pay purchases in retail locations, but it otherwise serves as an alternative to Apple Wallet. It can store payment cards for online checkout with Google Pay, and it syncs with Gmail and other Google apps for features like package tracking and storing tickets and boarding passes.<br/>
<br/>
As with Apple Wallet, Google Wallet lets users add loyalty and gym membership cards, so there's no need to use a physical card. Google says users can manage "agentic purchases made across Google," with easy access to order confirmations, receipts, and delivery updates.<br/>
<br/>
Apple began allowing NFC contactless payments in third-party apps with iOS 18.1, but it requires a commercial agreement with Apple, so that may be why Google hasn't implemented support. Google could add contactless payments, but it would need to pay Apple's fees. NFC access is available to app developers in Australia, Brazil, Canada, Japan, New Zealand, the U.K., and the U.S.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/google/">Google</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/google-wallet/">Google Wallet</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/google-wallet-iphone/">Google Wallet Available on iPhone, But Without Tap to Pay</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/google-wallet-available-on-iphone-but-without-tap-to-pay.2494673/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>